<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Asterisk on Typophile Archive</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/tags/asterisk/</link><description>Recent content in Asterisk on Typophile Archive</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 27 Dec 2007 02:50:00 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/tags/asterisk/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Asterisk</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/40347/</link><pubDate>Thu, 27 Dec 2007 02:50:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/40347/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A typographic symbol in the form of a star*, occupying space between the &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131016013416/http:/typophile.com/wiki/baseline"&gt;baseline&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131016013416/http:/typophile.com/wiki/ascender"&gt;ascender&lt;/a&gt; height, used as a reference mark for a &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131016013416/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Footnote"&gt;footnote&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131016013416/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Endnote"&gt;endnote&lt;/a&gt;, as illustrated by this example for the word &amp;ldquo;star&amp;rdquo; in the first line of text.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;* usually five-pointed or six-pointed&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>